1
00:00:01,401 --> 00:00:02,926
♪♪

2
00:02:05,025 --> 00:02:09,486
Joe, I'm certain you know
how difficult it must have been

3
00:02:09,630 --> 00:02:15,297
for Ginny to tell you that your
lovemaking... well, bores her.

4
00:02:15,435 --> 00:02:18,030
Difficult for her?
What about me?

5
00:02:21,975 --> 00:02:25,036
Well, we've made a
real breakthrough here.

6
00:02:25,178 --> 00:02:27,943
Next time, we'll build on it.

7
00:02:28,081 --> 00:02:30,641
Ginny, hug Joe.

8
00:02:38,492 --> 00:02:40,859
Joe, kiss Ginny.

9
00:02:42,763 --> 00:02:44,197
Don't start snoring.

10
00:02:48,135 --> 00:02:51,299
Your humor, Joe, is marvelous.

11
00:02:52,372 --> 00:02:54,034
And Ginny's honesty...

12
00:02:54,174 --> 00:02:59,135
I'm going to have to say you
kids make one heck of a couple.

13
00:02:59,279 --> 00:03:01,805
Now, I know you
probably don't realize this,

14
00:03:01,948 --> 00:03:04,679
but there was an awful
lot of love in this room.

15
00:03:08,155 --> 00:03:09,680
See you at 6?

16
00:03:23,670 --> 00:03:25,730
I'm having a crisis, Doctor.

17
00:03:25,872 --> 00:03:27,238
I need your help.

18
00:03:38,785 --> 00:03:42,085
No, Laura, not
here. Laura, not now.

19
00:03:42,222 --> 00:03:46,216
I checked your book.
You're clear for three hours.

20
00:03:46,359 --> 00:03:49,386
Stop it. Someone might come in.

21
00:03:55,569 --> 00:03:58,437
My place in 20 minutes?

22
00:04:20,994 --> 00:04:24,931
Okay, Ben, here we go...
Your life insurance needs.

23
00:04:25,065 --> 00:04:26,761
Now, are you aware
that your coverage

24
00:04:26,900 --> 00:04:30,701
should provide one to seven
times your annual income?

25
00:04:30,837 --> 00:04:34,098
Uh... Not to mention
your estate liquidity.

26
00:04:34,241 --> 00:04:36,870
Ben, you made a bundle
since my last review.

27
00:04:37,010 --> 00:04:39,377
You're going to need
additional coverage.

28
00:04:39,513 --> 00:04:43,143
But remember, I'm
not selling insurance.

29
00:04:43,283 --> 00:04:46,253
I'm selling peace of mind.

30
00:04:46,386 --> 00:04:52,087
How can you sleep knowing
your assets are uncovered?

31
00:04:52,225 --> 00:04:53,784
I didn't know they were.

32
00:04:53,927 --> 00:04:57,489
Do you have a copy of your parent
policy? We'll go over it line by line.

33
00:04:57,631 --> 00:04:59,122
I might even have one in here.

34
00:04:59,266 --> 00:05:00,586
No, I've got mine.
I've got mine.

35
00:05:00,667 --> 00:05:03,796
You stay here and keep talking.

36
00:05:03,937 --> 00:05:06,133
I think I saw it in
here yesterday.

37
00:05:06,273 --> 00:05:08,572
I was at a seminar
last year when...

38
00:05:09,743 --> 00:05:12,736
Please, dear God,
cut his tongue out.

39
00:05:12,879 --> 00:05:15,781
Let's see if it's in... No, no.

40
00:05:15,916 --> 00:05:20,479
Oh, I know. Here. Here,
here, here. Let's see. Yeah.

41
00:05:21,555 --> 00:05:24,024
Maybe, maybe, maybe, maybe.

42
00:05:24,157 --> 00:05:25,591
- Ben, I...
- Yeah.

43
00:05:26,960 --> 00:05:29,725
You want to maximize
your retirement benefits, Ben.

44
00:05:29,863 --> 00:05:31,889
Then there's our new
disability coverage.

45
00:05:32,032 --> 00:05:36,128
Chronic illness and severe injury can
strike men in your age group every day.

46
00:05:36,269 --> 00:05:39,762
With our policy, you can break every bone
in your body... even lose your members.

47
00:05:39,906 --> 00:05:41,272
My members?

48
00:05:41,408 --> 00:05:43,001
Arms, legs... you know.

49
00:05:43,143 --> 00:05:44,167
Members?

50
00:05:44,311 --> 00:05:47,281
Or you can go deaf, dumb,
and blind and get paid for it.

51
00:05:47,414 --> 00:05:49,576
My members?

52
00:05:49,716 --> 00:05:51,082
How's your wife?

53
00:05:51,218 --> 00:05:54,586
Oh, uh, Laura? She's great.

54
00:05:54,721 --> 00:05:57,452
Well, actually, we've
been having a little trouble.

55
00:05:57,591 --> 00:06:00,891
Started seeing a marriage
counselor... Dr. Fletcher. Terrific guy.

56
00:06:01,027 --> 00:06:02,667
He got right to the
heart of the problem.

57
00:06:02,796 --> 00:06:07,166
You see, Ben, Laura needs to
talk about her feelings, and I...

58
00:06:07,300 --> 00:06:09,360
Well, I have trouble
expressing myself.

59
00:06:09,502 --> 00:06:11,334
You do?

60
00:06:11,471 --> 00:06:13,372
Mmm.

61
00:06:21,414 --> 00:06:24,543
Oh, you were wonderful, Harding.

62
00:06:24,684 --> 00:06:26,243
Do you love me?

63
00:06:29,489 --> 00:06:31,424
Can't you tell?

64
00:06:34,694 --> 00:06:36,595
What was that?

65
00:06:46,306 --> 00:06:48,673
- It's Alan.
- Damn.

66
00:06:56,616 --> 00:06:58,517
Harding, the back door.

67
00:07:06,526 --> 00:07:08,825
Laura? Laura?

68
00:07:08,962 --> 00:07:10,055
Honey, are you home?

69
00:07:12,232 --> 00:07:16,363
Honey, aren't you supposed to be
in your group session at the clinic?

70
00:07:16,503 --> 00:07:18,904
Aren't you supposed
to be selling insurance?

71
00:07:19,039 --> 00:07:22,498
Well, I did. Ben Matlock just
bought and bought and bought.

72
00:07:22,642 --> 00:07:24,611
Why aren't you dressed?

73
00:07:24,744 --> 00:07:27,737
I'm showering... now.

74
00:07:27,881 --> 00:07:28,881
What?

75
00:07:28,915 --> 00:07:31,111
Laura?

76
00:07:47,600 --> 00:07:49,228
HF?

77
00:07:49,369 --> 00:07:51,600
HF.

78
00:07:51,738 --> 00:07:53,969
Harding Fletcher?

79
00:07:56,876 --> 00:07:58,777
Laura?

80
00:07:58,912 --> 00:08:00,676
Laura.

81
00:08:00,814 --> 00:08:02,806
- Laura!
- What is it?

82
00:08:02,949 --> 00:08:04,611
Harding Fletcher.

83
00:08:04,751 --> 00:08:07,016
I can explain.

84
00:08:07,153 --> 00:08:08,746
I only tried it once.

85
00:08:08,888 --> 00:08:10,322
You only tried it once?

86
00:08:10,457 --> 00:08:12,153
Tobacco.

87
00:08:12,292 --> 00:08:14,318
Wait. Wait. I'm spending
a fortune on a therapist

88
00:08:14,461 --> 00:08:15,588
so you can try his tobacco?

89
00:08:15,729 --> 00:08:17,163
He's saving our marriage.

90
00:08:17,297 --> 00:08:18,629
He's sleeping with my wife.

91
00:08:18,765 --> 00:08:20,256
Where are you going?

92
00:08:20,400 --> 00:08:23,461
Where a crazy person
goes... To see a shrink.

93
00:08:42,255 --> 00:08:43,348
Fletcher!

94
00:08:44,424 --> 00:08:46,359
- There's somebody in there.
- Huh.

95
00:08:46,493 --> 00:08:49,122
- Fletcher!
- Alan?

96
00:08:49,262 --> 00:08:51,424
You've been
sleeping with my wife.

97
00:08:51,564 --> 00:08:54,056
Alan, what are
you talking about?

98
00:08:54,200 --> 00:08:55,911
You know doggone well
what I'm talking about.

99
00:08:55,935 --> 00:08:57,279
You've been
sleeping with my wife.

100
00:08:57,303 --> 00:08:58,965
I found this under the bed.

101
00:09:03,009 --> 00:09:05,001
What a breakthrough.

102
00:09:05,145 --> 00:09:05,908
- Alan...
- What?

103
00:09:06,046 --> 00:09:09,039
You finally confronted the rage
you have against your father.

104
00:09:09,182 --> 00:09:10,241
Oh, come on.

105
00:09:10,383 --> 00:09:14,150
And even in this bizarre
situation, you are expressing it.

106
00:09:14,287 --> 00:09:16,188
- Bravo.
- You've been sleeping with my wife.

107
00:09:16,322 --> 00:09:18,223
This calls for a
private session.

108
00:09:18,358 --> 00:09:19,621
Well, you got that right.

109
00:09:19,759 --> 00:09:21,853
Uh, Tues... No,
Tuesday is no good.

110
00:09:21,995 --> 00:09:24,055
- Thursday, 6:30 p.m.?
- Yeah, 6:30.

111
00:09:24,197 --> 00:09:26,462
Yeah. Here. I hope
you get cancer.

112
00:09:26,599 --> 00:09:28,329
That's good. That is very good.

113
00:09:28,468 --> 00:09:29,663
Anger. Anger.

114
00:09:29,803 --> 00:09:31,328
Now, this is what
I want you to do...

115
00:09:31,471 --> 00:09:33,906
Hold on to that thought
until I see you Thursday.

116
00:09:34,040 --> 00:09:35,133
- But...
- Okay?

117
00:09:41,214 --> 00:09:42,375
Now...

118
00:09:46,352 --> 00:09:49,811
Next Wednesday, we'll begin
divorce counseling, hmm?

119
00:09:51,925 --> 00:09:52,984
Marshall...

120
00:09:56,663 --> 00:09:57,858
Hi.

121
00:10:13,179 --> 00:10:14,340
Wait.

122
00:10:16,316 --> 00:10:18,012
Alan, you're early.

123
00:10:19,719 --> 00:10:20,914
Oh, no.

124
00:10:21,054 --> 00:10:23,785
Now, now, wait a
minute. Just take it easy.

125
00:10:59,092 --> 00:11:00,617
Hey!

126
00:11:00,760 --> 00:11:02,160
What's going on?

127
00:11:13,106 --> 00:11:14,597
Hey!

128
00:11:20,713 --> 00:11:22,944
It doesn't look too
good for me, does it?

129
00:11:23,082 --> 00:11:26,575
You came flying out of an office
where a man has just been murdered

130
00:11:26,719 --> 00:11:28,688
and then ran from
the security guard.

131
00:11:28,821 --> 00:11:30,585
Could be worse,
but I don't know how.

132
00:11:30,723 --> 00:11:32,817
What about that guy that
was there just after me?

133
00:11:32,959 --> 00:11:34,052
Maybe he killed Fletcher.

134
00:11:34,194 --> 00:11:35,194
Fellow named Turner.

135
00:11:35,328 --> 00:11:40,266
The guard already verified that
Dr. Fletcher was alive when left.

136
00:11:40,400 --> 00:11:42,164
So I guess I'm the main suspect.

137
00:11:42,302 --> 00:11:45,136
You're the only suspect, Alan.

138
00:11:45,271 --> 00:11:47,069
Look at this arrest report.

139
00:11:47,207 --> 00:11:48,334
What?

140
00:11:48,474 --> 00:11:52,036
They read you your rights, told
you you didn't have to say anything,

141
00:11:52,178 --> 00:11:55,307
told you that whatever you
said would be used against you.

142
00:11:55,448 --> 00:11:56,507
Yeah, I remember that.

143
00:11:56,649 --> 00:11:59,049
The officer even asked me if I
understood what he was saying.

144
00:11:59,085 --> 00:12:01,554
That's because he couldn't
believe what you were saying.

145
00:12:01,688 --> 00:12:05,250
You told him that Dr. Fletcher
was having an affair with your wife

146
00:12:05,391 --> 00:12:08,623
and you burst into his office
furious and had words with him.

147
00:12:08,761 --> 00:12:10,821
And now they're using
what you said against you.

148
00:12:10,964 --> 00:12:13,092
I don't know
why I said all that.

149
00:12:13,233 --> 00:12:17,637
Alan, your mouth
is a big problem.

150
00:12:17,770 --> 00:12:18,829
Just when I'm nervous.

151
00:12:18,972 --> 00:12:21,840
You're nervous 25 hours a day.

152
00:12:21,975 --> 00:12:23,807
Why did you panic and run?

153
00:12:23,943 --> 00:12:25,912
When I saw Dr. Fletcher dead,

154
00:12:26,045 --> 00:12:28,310
I remembered this insurance
seminar on break-ins

155
00:12:28,448 --> 00:12:31,350
where it was pointed out that
after the scene of a shooting

156
00:12:31,484 --> 00:12:33,612
the culprit is often
still lying in wait.

157
00:12:33,753 --> 00:12:37,747
I remember this clearly because it
was either late May or early June of '87...

158
00:12:37,890 --> 00:12:40,490
Maybe it was '88... but it was
right after I was named Salesman...

159
00:12:40,526 --> 00:12:41,550
Alan.

160
00:12:45,732 --> 00:12:51,364
Who was there when you
burst into the doctor's office?

161
00:12:51,504 --> 00:12:54,303
A couple in session and a
woman in the waiting room.

162
00:12:54,440 --> 00:12:58,969
And they're the only ones who knew that
you were coming back on Thursday at 6:30?

163
00:12:59,112 --> 00:13:00,740
Yeah... and Laura.

164
00:13:02,348 --> 00:13:04,078
You told Laura?

165
00:13:05,184 --> 00:13:07,278
You're not going to
take my case, are you?

166
00:13:10,189 --> 00:13:13,717
Boy, I don't want to. Mm-mm.

167
00:13:15,061 --> 00:13:16,461
But I guess I will.

168
00:13:16,596 --> 00:13:17,996
You will?

169
00:13:18,131 --> 00:13:20,600
Yeah. As aggravating as you are,

170
00:13:20,733 --> 00:13:24,101
you couldn't kill anybody
unless you bored them to death.

171
00:13:24,237 --> 00:13:25,865
I'll make bail.

172
00:13:27,573 --> 00:13:29,542
How are you going to pay me?

173
00:13:29,676 --> 00:13:30,803
Oh, I don't know.

174
00:13:30,943 --> 00:13:33,572
Uh, selling insurance policies.

175
00:13:35,581 --> 00:13:37,675
It will take a car load.

176
00:13:52,532 --> 00:13:53,761
Alan.

177
00:14:07,146 --> 00:14:09,547
I was worried about you.

178
00:14:09,682 --> 00:14:11,674
Thanks for posting bail.

179
00:14:11,818 --> 00:14:15,016
You could have just
sent some tobacco over.

180
00:14:15,154 --> 00:14:18,522
Alan, I know you're upset.
It's okay if you take it out on me.

181
00:14:18,658 --> 00:14:20,718
- Well, that's hostile.
- You're hostile.

182
00:14:20,860 --> 00:14:22,726
- I'm not hostile.
- Hold it. Hold it. Hold it.

183
00:14:22,862 --> 00:14:24,006
- All I said was...
- I know what you said.

184
00:14:24,030 --> 00:14:26,022
- Hold it!
- I'm hurt, but I'm not hostile.

185
00:14:26,165 --> 00:14:27,428
Hold it!

186
00:14:27,567 --> 00:14:29,092
What's the matter with you?

187
00:14:29,235 --> 00:14:31,932
About to go on trial for murder
and all you can think about

188
00:14:32,071 --> 00:14:34,336
is being hurt and hostile
and fighting with your wife.

189
00:14:34,474 --> 00:14:36,667
- Now stop it.
- But I... Stop it!

190
00:14:38,778 --> 00:14:40,974
I want to ask you
some questions alone.

191
00:14:41,114 --> 00:14:42,707
- But...
- Alone.

192
00:14:44,117 --> 00:14:45,117
Okay.

193
00:14:46,753 --> 00:14:48,187
I'm not hostile.

194
00:14:51,557 --> 00:14:53,423
I'm hurt, but I'm not hostile.

195
00:14:57,263 --> 00:15:00,290
Did you have an affair
with Harding Fletcher?

196
00:15:01,734 --> 00:15:02,793
No.

197
00:15:02,935 --> 00:15:06,030
Of course, you wouldn't
tell me if you did.

198
00:15:07,874 --> 00:15:09,672
Of course I would.

199
00:15:10,910 --> 00:15:14,847
You're Alan's lawyer. I can't
help Alan if I don't tell you the truth.

200
00:15:14,981 --> 00:15:16,882
You want to help Alan?

201
00:15:17,016 --> 00:15:18,746
Of course.

202
00:15:20,686 --> 00:15:24,123
My relationship with Harding
Fletcher was strictly professional.

203
00:15:24,257 --> 00:15:29,321
He was a wonderful therapist...
Warm and caring and empathetic.

204
00:15:30,496 --> 00:15:32,692
Alan doesn't share your opinion.

205
00:15:35,301 --> 00:15:39,705
I was at a "for wives only" seminar
at the clinic the night Harding died.

206
00:15:39,839 --> 00:15:43,071
You should have seen
the outpouring of feelings.

207
00:15:43,209 --> 00:15:45,735
It was... amazing.

208
00:15:45,878 --> 00:15:47,073
Hmm.

209
00:15:47,213 --> 00:15:48,511
Anything else?

210
00:15:48,648 --> 00:15:51,277
Yeah. Be nice to Alan.

211
00:15:51,417 --> 00:15:55,354
No yelling, no fighting
till this thing's over.

212
00:15:55,488 --> 00:15:57,787
I understand.

213
00:15:57,924 --> 00:15:59,825
Alan arrested for murder.

214
00:16:01,194 --> 00:16:03,789
He's under a terrible strain.

215
00:16:03,930 --> 00:16:06,456
I'll be very supportive,
Mr. Matlock.

216
00:16:08,067 --> 00:16:11,003
He needs to concentrate
on what's important.

217
00:16:11,137 --> 00:16:12,537
His trial.

218
00:16:12,672 --> 00:16:14,800
Yeah, his trial.

219
00:16:16,576 --> 00:16:18,169
And insurance.

220
00:16:18,311 --> 00:16:22,442
He needs to sell
insurance, a lot of insurance.

221
00:16:26,586 --> 00:16:28,578
Why didn't anybody
hear the shots?

222
00:16:28,721 --> 00:16:31,384
All the rooms in the
clinic are sound-proofed.

223
00:16:31,524 --> 00:16:33,425
Well, I guess that makes sense.

224
00:16:33,559 --> 00:16:37,223
Well, you know, these people
paid this Dr. Fletcher a lot of money

225
00:16:37,363 --> 00:16:40,060
to have him listen to
them scream at each other.

226
00:16:40,199 --> 00:16:42,930
That's how they worked
out their differences.

227
00:16:43,069 --> 00:16:45,732
- Do you believe that?
- I don't know.

228
00:16:45,872 --> 00:16:47,534
You know, my parents did that.

229
00:16:47,673 --> 00:16:50,939
Yeah, they'd have a fight,
and he'd slam out the door,

230
00:16:51,077 --> 00:16:53,706
and an hour later he'd be back
bringing her some ice cream.

231
00:16:53,846 --> 00:16:55,314
Who needs a doctor, right?

232
00:16:55,448 --> 00:16:56,939
- I guess that makes sense.
- Yeah.

233
00:16:57,083 --> 00:16:59,245
You know, Dr. Fletcher
had a lot of patients.

234
00:16:59,385 --> 00:17:01,320
Where are his
files and his notes?

235
00:17:01,454 --> 00:17:04,481
Well, we didn't find
any... not one note.

236
00:17:04,624 --> 00:17:05,785
Hmm.

237
00:17:05,925 --> 00:17:07,621
No notes?

238
00:17:53,005 --> 00:17:55,702
No, no, no.

239
00:17:58,477 --> 00:18:01,208
Dr. Relkin?

240
00:18:01,347 --> 00:18:02,872
I'm Ben Matlock.

241
00:18:03,015 --> 00:18:04,415
Oh, yes.

242
00:18:04,550 --> 00:18:06,519
You're Alan Corning's attorney.

243
00:18:06,652 --> 00:18:09,486
How may I help you?
Tell him to stop that.

244
00:18:09,622 --> 00:18:11,750
See you on Thursday, Fred.

245
00:18:11,891 --> 00:18:15,328
Sorry. They think you're a new patient,
and they're welcoming you to the group.

246
00:18:15,461 --> 00:18:17,760
No, I don't think I'd fit in.

247
00:18:17,897 --> 00:18:20,196
I just want to ask a
couple of questions.

248
00:18:20,333 --> 00:18:25,033
You heard that Alan Corning
broke into Dr. Fletcher's office

249
00:18:25,171 --> 00:18:27,140
a few days before the murder?

250
00:18:27,273 --> 00:18:28,866
Everyone knew about that.

251
00:18:29,008 --> 00:18:32,877
I understand there was a couple in
session and a woman in the waiting room.

252
00:18:33,012 --> 00:18:35,846
Would you happen
to know who they are?

253
00:18:35,982 --> 00:18:39,350
I should. I keep a master
appointment list for billing purposes.

254
00:18:39,485 --> 00:18:43,445
Let's see...
Dr. Fletcher's patients.

255
00:18:43,589 --> 00:18:44,818
Here.

256
00:18:44,957 --> 00:18:47,324
The couple in session were
the Morells... Ginny and Joe.

257
00:18:47,460 --> 00:18:51,227
And the next patient... the woman in
the waiting room... was Claudette Hertz.

258
00:18:51,364 --> 00:18:54,596
See, the Morells and Mrs.
Hertz are scheduled today.

259
00:18:54,734 --> 00:18:56,100
Uh-huh.

260
00:18:57,503 --> 00:18:59,734
- Thank you.
- My pleasure.

261
00:19:22,695 --> 00:19:27,156
I'm looking for Joe
and Ginny Morell!

262
00:19:27,299 --> 00:19:29,097
I'm Ginny Morell.

263
00:19:31,771 --> 00:19:32,830
Is this...

264
00:19:33,906 --> 00:19:36,102
Is this a martial arts class?

265
00:19:36,242 --> 00:19:37,733
No, this is therapy.

266
00:19:37,877 --> 00:19:41,336
I heard that you and
your husband knew

267
00:19:41,480 --> 00:19:45,941
that Alan Corning was going
to be in Dr. Fletcher's office

268
00:19:46,085 --> 00:19:47,986
at 6:30 the night of the murder.

269
00:19:48,120 --> 00:19:49,383
Correct?

270
00:19:49,522 --> 00:19:50,820
Yes, okay?

271
00:19:50,956 --> 00:19:53,755
We knew that he had an
appointment with Dr. Fletcher.

272
00:19:53,893 --> 00:19:56,658
If we'd only known that he
was going to murder Dr. Fletcher,

273
00:19:56,796 --> 00:19:58,890
Joe would have
never gone out of town.

274
00:19:59,031 --> 00:20:01,466
I would not have gone to
the "for wives only" seminar.

275
00:20:03,202 --> 00:20:06,798
I mean, Dr. Fletcher saved
our marriage, Mr. Matlock,

276
00:20:06,939 --> 00:20:08,979
and I don't know what
we're going to do without him.

277
00:20:09,108 --> 00:20:12,374
Well, maybe you'll find
another Dr. Fletcher.

278
00:20:12,511 --> 00:20:15,538
No. There's only
one Dr. Fletcher.

279
00:20:15,681 --> 00:20:18,617
Well, just keep
plenty of these things

280
00:20:18,751 --> 00:20:21,880
and just kick the living...
you know... Out of them.

281
00:20:24,090 --> 00:20:26,457
It's like the Marx Brothers.

282
00:20:36,569 --> 00:20:39,562
Aah!

283
00:20:39,705 --> 00:20:43,870
Aah! Aah!

284
00:20:44,009 --> 00:20:45,910
Aah!

285
00:20:46,045 --> 00:20:50,915
Aah! Aah!

286
00:20:51,050 --> 00:20:52,450
What's the matter?

287
00:20:52,585 --> 00:20:53,848
I'm screaming.

288
00:20:53,986 --> 00:20:55,181
I know.

289
00:20:55,321 --> 00:20:57,256
It's primal screaming.

290
00:20:57,389 --> 00:20:59,984
Oh. Oh, oh.

291
00:21:00,126 --> 00:21:02,561
Does your husband
scream with you?

292
00:21:02,695 --> 00:21:04,926
My husband's gone.

293
00:21:05,064 --> 00:21:06,760
I'm sorry. How old was he?

294
00:21:06,899 --> 00:21:08,993
He's not dead. We're divorcing.

295
00:21:09,135 --> 00:21:13,163
Aah! Aah!

296
00:21:13,305 --> 00:21:18,801
Dr. Fletcher showed us that we
didn't belong together, so we parted.

297
00:21:18,944 --> 00:21:22,642
Aah! Aah!

298
00:21:22,782 --> 00:21:25,377
But Dr. Fletcher stood by me.

299
00:21:25,518 --> 00:21:31,082
He gave me strength,
support, self-esteem.

300
00:21:31,223 --> 00:21:32,384
Good.

301
00:21:32,525 --> 00:21:34,255
I have to ask you...

302
00:21:34,393 --> 00:21:36,362
- No, don't do that.
- I have to.

303
00:21:36,495 --> 00:21:38,054
- No, you can't!
- I must!

304
00:21:38,197 --> 00:21:41,793
- I have to ask you where you were...
- Aah!

305
00:21:41,934 --> 00:21:43,163
- No. No.
- Aah!

306
00:21:43,302 --> 00:21:46,101
I'm sorry. I'm sorry. I
don't mean to upset you.

307
00:21:46,238 --> 00:21:47,262
Waah!

308
00:21:47,406 --> 00:21:50,137
Will you stop screaming?
You're starting to hurt my throat!

309
00:21:51,610 --> 00:21:54,842
I was at the "wives
only" seminar.

310
00:21:54,980 --> 00:21:57,950
Aah! Aah!

311
00:21:58,083 --> 00:21:59,881
You have a lovely scream.

312
00:22:00,019 --> 00:22:01,487
Thank you for sharing.

313
00:22:01,620 --> 00:22:02,918
Aah!

314
00:22:10,696 --> 00:22:13,632
Ben, I just got to
Dr. Fletcher's house.

315
00:22:13,766 --> 00:22:16,201
Yeah, I'll let you
know what I find.

316
00:22:16,335 --> 00:22:17,564
Goodbye.

317
00:24:17,556 --> 00:24:21,186
When I got to Dr. Fletcher's house,
I knew someone was already there.

318
00:24:21,327 --> 00:24:23,353
And sure enough,
out comes this blonde

319
00:24:23,495 --> 00:24:27,728
carrying a leather and rhinestone
jacket and a diamond bracelet.

320
00:24:27,866 --> 00:24:29,459
- Blonde, huh?
- Yeah.

321
00:24:29,601 --> 00:24:34,130
Yea tall, beautiful,
hair cut to about here.

322
00:24:34,273 --> 00:24:36,071
That's Laura... Alan's wife.

323
00:24:36,208 --> 00:24:37,335
Right.

324
00:24:37,476 --> 00:24:40,241
So then I followed her
to this fancy apartment

325
00:24:40,379 --> 00:24:44,475
where this great-looking
brunette comes to the door.

326
00:24:44,616 --> 00:24:45,616
Kind of curly?

327
00:24:45,718 --> 00:24:46,515
Yeah.

328
00:24:46,652 --> 00:24:50,054
That's Claudette
Hertz. Then what?

329
00:24:50,189 --> 00:24:55,685
Then the tall blonde gave the
diamond bracelet to the curly brunette.

330
00:24:55,828 --> 00:24:58,195
- Then what?
- That's it.

331
00:24:58,330 --> 00:24:59,457
Now what?

332
00:25:02,267 --> 00:25:05,701
Uh... I like to talk to blondes.

333
00:25:07,473 --> 00:25:10,238
How did you know I was
at Dr. Fletcher's house?

334
00:25:11,877 --> 00:25:13,903
You were having me followed.

335
00:25:14,046 --> 00:25:15,742
Well, certainly.

336
00:25:15,881 --> 00:25:19,318
What was going on
between you and Dr. Fletcher?

337
00:25:19,451 --> 00:25:21,784
I already told you... nothing.

338
00:25:21,920 --> 00:25:23,821
I don't believe you.

339
00:25:23,956 --> 00:25:26,118
Then why don't you tell me?

340
00:25:26,258 --> 00:25:29,695
I think you and Dr. Fletcher
were having an affair

341
00:25:29,828 --> 00:25:33,697
and you took incriminating
evidence from his house...

342
00:25:33,832 --> 00:25:35,858
The jacket and the bracelet.

343
00:25:37,369 --> 00:25:38,928
I'm not talking to
you, Mr. Matlock.

344
00:25:39,071 --> 00:25:40,699
Then I'll just talk
to your husband.

345
00:25:40,839 --> 00:25:42,307
You would tell Alan?

346
00:25:42,441 --> 00:25:43,807
Well, certainly.

347
00:25:43,942 --> 00:25:47,845
I have to be honest with
him, and Alan already knows.

348
00:25:50,149 --> 00:25:51,515
All right.

349
00:25:53,185 --> 00:25:56,280
I was having an affair
with Harding Fletcher.

350
00:25:57,756 --> 00:26:03,218
I was feeling alienated and vulnerable,
and Harding had a need to nurture.

351
00:26:03,362 --> 00:26:04,489
Do you understand?

352
00:26:04,630 --> 00:26:07,156
Sure. You were
hot for each other.

353
00:26:10,035 --> 00:26:12,004
The affair was a mistake.

354
00:26:12,137 --> 00:26:13,161
I love Alan.

355
00:26:13,305 --> 00:26:18,039
I wouldn't want to hurt him, so I went
to Harding's place and got my things.

356
00:26:18,177 --> 00:26:21,375
You took a jacket and
a bracelet from his place

357
00:26:21,513 --> 00:26:25,575
and then went to Claudette Hertz'
apartment and gave her the bracelet.

358
00:26:25,717 --> 00:26:26,878
Why would you do that?

359
00:26:29,221 --> 00:26:31,087
Claudette's a
dear friend of mine,

360
00:26:31,223 --> 00:26:34,625
and the bracelet had sad
memories for me, so I gave it to her.

361
00:26:35,761 --> 00:26:38,526
Well, if you and Claudette
are such dear friends,

362
00:26:38,664 --> 00:26:40,997
why didn't Alan recognize
her in the waiting room?

363
00:26:43,836 --> 00:26:46,704
Claudette and I became
friends at a women's group.

364
00:26:46,839 --> 00:26:48,171
Alan never met her.

365
00:26:50,542 --> 00:26:52,033
Okay.

366
00:26:54,780 --> 00:26:57,750
I know you have to defend him,

367
00:26:57,883 --> 00:26:59,923
but you don't have to cause
him any additional pain.

368
00:26:59,952 --> 00:27:01,750
You don't have to tell him.

369
00:27:01,887 --> 00:27:04,220
Well, Alan...

370
00:27:05,457 --> 00:27:07,585
Well, we'll see.

371
00:27:25,511 --> 00:27:26,511
Here you go.

372
00:27:26,612 --> 00:27:28,171
Hmm. Oh, thank you.

373
00:27:28,313 --> 00:27:30,339
Oh, that's a beautiful bracelet.

374
00:27:30,482 --> 00:27:31,609
Yes, it is.

375
00:27:31,750 --> 00:27:33,241
Nice of Laura to give it to you.

376
00:27:33,385 --> 00:27:34,385
How many carats?

377
00:27:34,486 --> 00:27:36,114
Five-something.

378
00:27:37,756 --> 00:27:41,693
Women don't give other
women $10,000 bracelets.

379
00:27:41,827 --> 00:27:43,557
Actually, she just
loaned it to me.

380
00:27:43,695 --> 00:27:44,695
Oh.

381
00:27:45,931 --> 00:27:47,451
Well, that doesn't
make sense, either.

382
00:27:47,533 --> 00:27:51,994
I mean, if she didn't want to wear
it or even look at it, it's too valuable.

383
00:27:52,137 --> 00:27:57,132
She would have put it away
or... Like in a safety deposit box.

384
00:27:57,276 --> 00:28:02,874
Uh, unless it's yours.

385
00:28:04,683 --> 00:28:06,208
What are you talking about?

386
00:28:06,351 --> 00:28:09,879
Well, suppose you left that
bracelet at Dr. Fletcher's house,

387
00:28:10,022 --> 00:28:12,992
and Laura picked it up for you
when she went to get her jacket.

388
00:28:13,125 --> 00:28:16,254
I've never been to
Dr. Fletcher's house,

389
00:28:16,395 --> 00:28:18,626
and I resent the insinuation.

390
00:28:18,764 --> 00:28:20,289
Well, I'm sure you do.

391
00:28:20,432 --> 00:28:22,367
But when things don't
make sense to me...

392
00:28:22,501 --> 00:28:25,403
Like Laura giving you that
bracelet or loaning it to you...

393
00:28:25,537 --> 00:28:29,838
Then my mind goes to
explanations that do make sense.

394
00:28:31,076 --> 00:28:32,840
I'll show you out, Mr. Matlock.

395
00:28:33,879 --> 00:28:34,938
Okay.

396
00:28:36,515 --> 00:28:38,541
Oh, that's a shame.

397
00:28:38,684 --> 00:28:39,982
Something wrong?

398
00:28:40,118 --> 00:28:43,953
I've got a carpet cleaner that
can lift that right out of your rug.

399
00:28:44,089 --> 00:28:46,422
I've already called one.

400
00:28:46,558 --> 00:28:48,049
Oh, good.

401
00:28:48,193 --> 00:28:49,957
Have a nice day.

402
00:28:55,534 --> 00:28:58,936
Laura Corning and Claudette
Hertz both lied to me.

403
00:29:00,172 --> 00:29:01,333
- Both of them?
- Yeah.

404
00:29:01,473 --> 00:29:05,103
Laura Corning had an
affair with Dr. Fletcher.

405
00:29:05,244 --> 00:29:06,542
Oh.

406
00:29:06,678 --> 00:29:10,115
Alan's wife was having an affair
with their marriage counselor?

407
00:29:10,249 --> 00:29:14,016
Yeah. And I'm sure that Claudette
Hertz did, too, but she wouldn't admit it.

408
00:29:14,152 --> 00:29:16,781
Wow.

409
00:29:17,956 --> 00:29:20,585
Dr. Fletcher knew about
what comes naturally.

410
00:29:20,726 --> 00:29:23,662
Yeah. He was giving out a little
more than advice, wasn't he?

411
00:29:23,795 --> 00:29:27,630
So I guess one of the
ladies figured it out and...

412
00:29:27,766 --> 00:29:29,029
Think that's what happened?

413
00:29:29,167 --> 00:29:31,398
They both lied to me,
Conrad, about everything.

414
00:29:31,536 --> 00:29:34,301
So I think they lied
about their alibis.

415
00:29:34,439 --> 00:29:37,466
Doing what comes
naturally with two?

416
00:29:38,744 --> 00:29:40,542
Put a man on thin ice.

417
00:29:40,679 --> 00:29:42,375
Yeah.

418
00:29:42,514 --> 00:29:49,944
How about tomorrow we stop by
that marriage counseling place?

419
00:29:58,063 --> 00:30:00,294
So good to see you, Mr. Matlock.

420
00:30:00,432 --> 00:30:01,866
Conrad, this is Dr. Relkin.

421
00:30:03,035 --> 00:30:05,027
You're no stranger to hugging.

422
00:30:05,170 --> 00:30:06,001
No, I'm not.

423
00:30:06,138 --> 00:30:08,630
Everybody in my family hugs
everybody else all the time.

424
00:30:08,774 --> 00:30:10,800
How healthy. How wonderful.

425
00:30:10,942 --> 00:30:12,843
Has your family always hugged,

426
00:30:12,978 --> 00:30:16,346
or was there a significant event
that precipitated the behavior?

427
00:30:17,749 --> 00:30:19,877
Well, let me see...

428
00:30:21,553 --> 00:30:26,150
While Conrad tries to remember,
I'd like to ask some questions.

429
00:30:26,291 --> 00:30:28,226
Laura Corning and
Claudette Hertz have said

430
00:30:28,360 --> 00:30:31,091
that they were in your
"for wives only" seminar

431
00:30:31,229 --> 00:30:33,198
at the time Dr. Fletcher
was murdered.

432
00:30:33,332 --> 00:30:34,732
Is that your recollection?

433
00:30:34,866 --> 00:30:37,165
That seminar was packed.

434
00:30:37,302 --> 00:30:40,534
I was worried I hadn't mimeoed
enough questionnaires to go around,

435
00:30:40,672 --> 00:30:44,165
but I definitely remember
seeing Claudette and Laura there.

436
00:30:45,711 --> 00:30:48,510
If you gentlemen will excuse
me, I have to start a group session.

437
00:30:48,647 --> 00:30:50,741
Oh, Doctor, we always hugged.

438
00:30:50,882 --> 00:30:52,578
- Good.
- Yeah.

439
00:30:52,718 --> 00:30:54,653
Good.

440
00:30:54,786 --> 00:30:58,223
Very good.

441
00:30:59,291 --> 00:31:01,954
See, Ben, hugging is
why I grew up to be so nice.

442
00:31:02,094 --> 00:31:03,995
You'd fit right in here.

443
00:31:04,129 --> 00:31:06,325
- There's the jacket.
- What jacket?

444
00:31:06,465 --> 00:31:09,492
That's the jacket I saw Laura
Corning carry from Dr. Fletcher's house.

445
00:31:09,634 --> 00:31:11,159
That's Ginny Morell.

446
00:31:11,303 --> 00:31:12,703
That makes three of them.

447
00:31:12,838 --> 00:31:14,067
- Three?
- Yeah.

448
00:31:14,206 --> 00:31:15,731
Give me a minute.

449
00:31:22,447 --> 00:31:25,349
You're wearing
Laura Corning's jacket.

450
00:31:25,484 --> 00:31:26,816
It's my jacket.

451
00:31:26,952 --> 00:31:30,821
Laura told me she left that
jacket at Dr. Fletcher's house.

452
00:31:30,956 --> 00:31:34,085
I loaned it to Laura before
Dr. Fletcher was murdered.

453
00:31:34,226 --> 00:31:36,218
You're sure you didn't
leave it there yourself?

454
00:31:36,361 --> 00:31:40,321
Hey, look, I spent four
years and $50,000 in therapy

455
00:31:40,465 --> 00:31:42,866
because my father was
a nosy old coot like you.

456
00:31:43,001 --> 00:31:46,904
So I'm not answering any more of
your questions, Pops... like it or lump it.

457
00:31:47,038 --> 00:31:49,633
Move. I'm late for
my sensitivity class.

458
00:31:53,478 --> 00:31:54,478
Hi.

459
00:31:54,546 --> 00:31:55,707
Hi yourself.

460
00:31:57,549 --> 00:31:58,744
How did it go?

461
00:32:00,619 --> 00:32:04,283
That woman you were so
nice to just called me Pops.

462
00:32:04,423 --> 00:32:05,652
That's awful.

463
00:32:05,791 --> 00:32:07,692
That's just awful, Pops.

464
00:32:11,163 --> 00:32:17,160
I think that is her jacket, and I think
she left it in Dr. Fletcher's house.

465
00:32:17,302 --> 00:32:19,567
You really think he was
having affairs with three women?

466
00:32:19,704 --> 00:32:21,570
Laura said he was nurturing.

467
00:32:21,706 --> 00:32:24,335
I think he nurtured
like a big bunny rabbit.

468
00:32:24,476 --> 00:32:26,172
One of them killed him.

469
00:32:28,079 --> 00:32:30,514
Maybe each of them
found out about the others.

470
00:32:30,649 --> 00:32:31,776
Yeah.

471
00:32:31,917 --> 00:32:36,621
A woman scorned...
More than that...

472
00:32:36,755 --> 00:32:42,922
Three patients scorned and
manipulated in a very unethical way

473
00:32:43,061 --> 00:32:46,395
by a doctor who has
sworn to try to help them.

474
00:32:46,531 --> 00:32:49,330
And all this jerk
did was use them.

475
00:32:50,469 --> 00:32:52,734
Doing what comes naturally.

476
00:32:52,871 --> 00:32:55,067
He did it a little
too well, didn't he?

477
00:33:07,385 --> 00:33:10,184
We've been over
this place three times.

478
00:33:10,322 --> 00:33:12,120
We're not going
to find those notes.

479
00:33:12,257 --> 00:33:13,850
Yeah, I guess you're right.

480
00:33:13,992 --> 00:33:15,654
We might as well go.

481
00:33:15,794 --> 00:33:19,629
I've got a feeling those
notes would make all the...

482
00:33:22,000 --> 00:33:24,162
All the difference.

483
00:33:27,973 --> 00:33:29,441
- Wait.
- Wait a minute.

484
00:33:34,813 --> 00:33:38,443
There's Dr. Fletcher
in his office.

485
00:33:43,188 --> 00:33:49,128
Mrs. Morell, you and your husband were
in marriage counseling with Dr. Fletcher.

486
00:33:49,261 --> 00:33:50,261
Correct?

487
00:33:50,328 --> 00:33:51,352
Yes, we were.

488
00:33:51,496 --> 00:33:53,294
And you also saw him alone?

489
00:33:53,431 --> 00:33:55,593
No, only with Joe.

490
00:33:55,734 --> 00:33:58,727
You never once went
alone to his house?

491
00:33:58,870 --> 00:34:00,702
No, of course not.

492
00:34:00,839 --> 00:34:05,834
Do you deny that you left an
expensive jacket at his house?

493
00:34:05,977 --> 00:34:09,311
I never left any jacket
because I was never there.

494
00:34:09,447 --> 00:34:12,007
Do you deny the
jacket was there?

495
00:34:14,019 --> 00:34:17,114
Well, no. I loaned the
jacket to somebody.

496
00:34:17,255 --> 00:34:19,815
I can only assume
that she left it there.

497
00:34:19,958 --> 00:34:21,984
Oh. Uh, Laura Corning?

498
00:34:22,127 --> 00:34:24,028
- Yes.
- Uh-huh.

499
00:34:24,162 --> 00:34:27,530
Uh, Mrs. Morell, is, uh...

500
00:34:30,435 --> 00:34:33,098
is this your jacket?

501
00:34:33,238 --> 00:34:34,238
Yes.

502
00:34:34,306 --> 00:34:37,299
It's very beautiful.
Very... Very expensive.

503
00:34:37,442 --> 00:34:39,570
Look at that. Mmm.

504
00:34:39,711 --> 00:34:41,407
What size would you say it is?

505
00:34:41,546 --> 00:34:46,314
Oh, it's right here on
the label, size 6 petite.

506
00:34:46,451 --> 00:34:48,511
You're a very small
woman, aren't you?

507
00:34:49,621 --> 00:34:51,249
- Petite.
- Of course.

508
00:34:51,389 --> 00:34:54,917
You say you loaned this
jacket to Laura Corning?

509
00:34:55,060 --> 00:34:56,084
Yes.

510
00:34:56,227 --> 00:34:57,787
Is Mrs. Corning in
the courtroom today?

511
00:34:57,829 --> 00:34:58,922
Yes.

512
00:34:59,064 --> 00:35:00,862
Would you point her out, please?

513
00:35:03,134 --> 00:35:05,865
Mrs. Corning, would
you please stand up?

514
00:35:08,573 --> 00:35:09,905
Huh.

515
00:35:11,343 --> 00:35:12,436
Thank you.

516
00:35:14,913 --> 00:35:21,513
Mrs. Corning is a fairly tall
lady, a little larger than you.

517
00:35:21,653 --> 00:35:25,556
Why would she borrow a
jacket that was too small for her?

518
00:35:27,192 --> 00:35:29,024
I don't know.

519
00:35:29,160 --> 00:35:31,823
Mrs. Corning didn't
wear this jacket

520
00:35:31,963 --> 00:35:34,558
and didn't leave it at Dr. Fletcher's
house. You must have.

521
00:35:34,699 --> 00:35:37,100
You were there, and you
left the jacket, didn't you?

522
00:35:37,235 --> 00:35:39,966
Objection. Your
Honor, this is irrelevant.

523
00:35:40,105 --> 00:35:43,238
Sustained. Mr. Matlock...
But, Your Honor...

524
00:35:43,375 --> 00:35:46,573
Objection sustained.
Now please move on.

525
00:35:48,680 --> 00:35:50,239
No further questions.

526
00:35:51,249 --> 00:35:56,586
Mrs. Corning, you and your
husband were in marriage counseling

527
00:35:56,721 --> 00:35:59,054
with the late Dr. Fletcher,
is that correct?

528
00:35:59,190 --> 00:36:00,351
Yes.

529
00:36:00,492 --> 00:36:02,051
And at the same time,

530
00:36:02,193 --> 00:36:07,325
you were having an affair with
the late Dr. Fletcher, weren't you?

531
00:36:07,465 --> 00:36:08,763
Yes.

532
00:36:08,900 --> 00:36:12,132
And when you found out that
Ginny Morell and Claudette Hertz

533
00:36:12,270 --> 00:36:15,798
were also having affairs
with the late Dr. Fletcher,

534
00:36:15,940 --> 00:36:19,536
did that make you feel
angry and deceived?

535
00:36:19,678 --> 00:36:22,375
I don't know anything
about Ginny or Claudette,

536
00:36:22,514 --> 00:36:24,558
but if you're saying I got jealous
and killed him, I have witnesses.

537
00:36:24,582 --> 00:36:28,815
Oh, I know. You were at
the "for wives only" seminar.

538
00:36:28,953 --> 00:36:33,857
But sometime after that,

539
00:36:33,992 --> 00:36:38,930
didn't you break into Dr. Fletcher's
house and remove a jacket and a bracelet?

540
00:36:39,064 --> 00:36:40,555
I didn't break in. I had a key.

541
00:36:42,167 --> 00:36:43,396
I don't get it.

542
00:36:43,535 --> 00:36:44,935
You had a key.

543
00:36:45,070 --> 00:36:49,906
You let yourself into Dr. Fletcher's
house after the murder

544
00:36:50,041 --> 00:36:53,307
and removed a jacket
belonging to Mrs. Morell

545
00:36:53,445 --> 00:36:57,212
and an expensive bracelet
belonging to Claudette Hertz.

546
00:36:57,348 --> 00:37:03,618
Why would you risk going back
into that house after the murder

547
00:37:03,755 --> 00:37:08,056
to remove evidence that obviously
incriminated people other than yourself?

548
00:37:10,628 --> 00:37:15,089
Well, I wasn't sure that I had all
of my things out of there or not,

549
00:37:15,233 --> 00:37:19,568
and so, when I
discovered that I had,

550
00:37:19,704 --> 00:37:22,333
I found Ginny's jacket
and Claudette's bracelet.

551
00:37:22,474 --> 00:37:24,074
Well, they're very
dear friends of mine.

552
00:37:24,175 --> 00:37:27,509
I don't think either one of them
had an affair with Dr. Fletcher.

553
00:37:27,645 --> 00:37:30,809
And so I decided to remove
their things, you know,

554
00:37:30,949 --> 00:37:32,281
so they wouldn't be compromised.

555
00:37:34,853 --> 00:37:37,152
I see... I...

556
00:37:38,289 --> 00:37:39,689
I think.

557
00:37:39,824 --> 00:37:43,395
But, uh... Well,
nothing further.

558
00:37:43,528 --> 00:37:49,365
Mrs. Hertz, did you leave a diamond
bracelet at Dr. Fletcher's house?

559
00:37:49,501 --> 00:37:51,163
You know I did.

560
00:37:51,302 --> 00:37:54,602
Laura Corning says that she
removed that bracelet from his house

561
00:37:54,739 --> 00:37:56,731
so that you wouldn't
be compromised.

562
00:37:56,875 --> 00:38:01,745
She said she did it out of her
deep and everlasting friendship

563
00:38:01,880 --> 00:38:04,611
with you and Ginny
Morell. Is that true?

564
00:38:04,749 --> 00:38:07,218
Yes. The three of
us are very close.

565
00:38:07,352 --> 00:38:09,378
Well, you had a lot in common.

566
00:38:09,521 --> 00:38:11,615
You were all having
marital problems,

567
00:38:11,756 --> 00:38:13,122
you were all in the clinic,

568
00:38:13,258 --> 00:38:16,251
and you were all having affairs
with Dr. Fletcher, weren't you?

569
00:38:16,394 --> 00:38:17,726
That's a lie.

570
00:38:17,862 --> 00:38:21,128
You didn't know of one
another's affairs with him

571
00:38:21,266 --> 00:38:26,261
until the morning Alan Corning
came bursting into the office,

572
00:38:26,404 --> 00:38:29,806
yelling at the good doctor
for fooling around with his wife.

573
00:38:29,941 --> 00:38:32,638
That's the day that you
and Ginny Morell found out

574
00:38:32,777 --> 00:38:35,178
the doctor had been
cheating on you, wasn't it?

575
00:38:35,313 --> 00:38:37,305
That's absurd.

576
00:38:37,448 --> 00:38:42,386
Did you feel a little angry when
you found out you'd been deceived?

577
00:38:42,520 --> 00:38:45,888
I'm not stupid, Mr. Matlock. I
know what you're leading up to.

578
00:38:46,024 --> 00:38:48,459
I did not kill Dr. Fletcher.

579
00:38:48,593 --> 00:38:50,805
- I was at the "wives only" seminar.
- "Wives only" seminar.

580
00:38:50,829 --> 00:38:51,829
Yeah, yeah.

581
00:38:51,896 --> 00:38:55,298
The three of you are each other's
witnesses, but somebody's lying.

582
00:38:55,433 --> 00:38:59,302
Objection. Counsel has ceased
asking questions and begun ruminating.

583
00:38:59,437 --> 00:39:03,238
Uh, Your Honor, the
questions are coming, I promise.

584
00:39:03,374 --> 00:39:06,742
- They're coming, Your Honor.
- Well, let's hear them, then, Mr. Matlock.

585
00:39:06,878 --> 00:39:08,608
- Objection overruled.
- Thank you.

586
00:39:08,746 --> 00:39:10,214
Who could be lying?

587
00:39:10,348 --> 00:39:12,817
Who killed Dr. Fletcher?

588
00:39:12,951 --> 00:39:17,286
And it took me a
while to figure it out,

589
00:39:17,422 --> 00:39:22,258
but I finally realized the
only way I could know

590
00:39:22,393 --> 00:39:26,524
was to find Dr. Fletcher's
personal notes.

591
00:39:26,664 --> 00:39:29,657
Now, do you have any idea what
happened to those personal notes?

592
00:39:29,801 --> 00:39:31,133
None at all.

593
00:39:31,269 --> 00:39:33,500
Neither does anybody
else, seemingly.

594
00:39:33,638 --> 00:39:37,439
I looked for them and looked for them and
looked for them, and I couldn't find them.

595
00:39:37,575 --> 00:39:42,309
But I finally... I finally figured
out where they had been...

596
00:39:42,447 --> 00:39:46,817
In a safe in
Dr. Fletcher's office.

597
00:39:46,951 --> 00:39:49,785
Now, do you know
where that safe turned up?

598
00:39:49,921 --> 00:39:52,186
- I have no idea.
- Huh.

599
00:39:52,323 --> 00:39:54,519
It was in your
apartment, wasn't it?

600
00:39:54,659 --> 00:39:57,629
That's ridiculous. There's
no safe in my apartment.

601
00:39:57,762 --> 00:39:59,526
No, no, no.

602
00:39:59,664 --> 00:40:02,828
There's no safe in
your apartment now.

603
00:40:03,902 --> 00:40:06,030
It was. Not now.

604
00:40:06,170 --> 00:40:08,730
Now it's here.

605
00:40:08,873 --> 00:40:11,672
Uh, thank you, Mr. McMasters.

606
00:40:11,809 --> 00:40:16,008
Your Honor, could we mark
this safe Defense Exhibit C?

607
00:40:16,147 --> 00:40:20,812
Is this the safe that
was in your apartment?

608
00:40:22,186 --> 00:40:23,882
I never saw it before.

609
00:40:24,022 --> 00:40:26,719
And you were in my apartment.
You didn't see it there, either.

610
00:40:26,858 --> 00:40:28,793
No, I didn't. I didn't.

611
00:40:28,927 --> 00:40:31,556
But I know it had been in there.

612
00:40:31,696 --> 00:40:33,358
You know how I know?

613
00:40:33,498 --> 00:40:38,198
By the rust indentations
on your brand-new rug.

614
00:40:38,336 --> 00:40:42,330
I got to thinking, here you are in
a new apartment with a new rug,

615
00:40:42,473 --> 00:40:44,533
and yet something had
already been moved out.

616
00:40:44,676 --> 00:40:47,703
Now, how did those rust
indentations get in your rug?

617
00:40:47,845 --> 00:40:49,108
I don't know.

618
00:40:49,247 --> 00:40:52,877
Dr. Fletcher had the
same rust indentations...

619
00:40:54,385 --> 00:40:56,377
on a rug in the corner...

620
00:40:58,356 --> 00:41:00,416
of his office. You see there?

621
00:41:00,558 --> 00:41:02,459
See that? See that?

622
00:41:02,593 --> 00:41:09,090
Let's see, let's mark this
picture Defense Exhibit D.

623
00:41:09,233 --> 00:41:11,168
It was hanging in
Dr. Fletcher's office.

624
00:41:11,302 --> 00:41:13,737
See, this is a picture
of Dr. Fletcher,

625
00:41:13,871 --> 00:41:18,809
his office furniture,
including the safe... see?

626
00:41:18,943 --> 00:41:20,036
There.

627
00:41:20,178 --> 00:41:25,344
Now, let's mark this
photo Defense Exhibit E,

628
00:41:25,483 --> 00:41:28,351
taken at the scene of
the crime after the murder.

629
00:41:28,486 --> 00:41:32,651
Now see? Same
office furniture, no safe.

630
00:41:32,790 --> 00:41:35,885
See? No safe.

631
00:41:37,628 --> 00:41:39,494
What happened to
the safe, Mrs. Hertz?

632
00:41:39,630 --> 00:41:41,997
I don't know what
you're talking about.

633
00:41:42,133 --> 00:41:46,969
Your building superintendent,
Mr. Anthony Giarelli,

634
00:41:47,105 --> 00:41:50,098
you do remember
slipping him $100

635
00:41:50,241 --> 00:41:52,335
to get that safe out of
your apartment in a hurry

636
00:41:52,477 --> 00:41:54,969
the day you found out I was
coming out for a visit, don't you?

637
00:41:55,113 --> 00:41:56,638
No.

638
00:41:56,781 --> 00:41:59,683
Laura Corning called you
and told you, didn't she?

639
00:41:59,817 --> 00:42:01,547
Absolutely not.

640
00:42:01,686 --> 00:42:05,555
If I told you that Mr. Giarelli's
in the courtroom today,

641
00:42:05,690 --> 00:42:07,249
would that improve
your recollection?

642
00:42:07,392 --> 00:42:09,486
Would you stand
up, Mr. Giarelli?

643
00:42:16,334 --> 00:42:17,893
Now do you remember?

644
00:42:20,238 --> 00:42:21,968
It's not what you think.

645
00:42:22,106 --> 00:42:26,635
You don't know what
I think, so I'll tell you.

646
00:42:26,778 --> 00:42:32,740
I think you, Ginny Morell,
Laura Corning got together

647
00:42:32,884 --> 00:42:38,551
and realized that Dr. Fletcher
had probably kept notes

648
00:42:38,689 --> 00:42:40,317
on his affairs with you.

649
00:42:40,458 --> 00:42:44,259
Now, Ginny Morell and Laura Corning
have husbands. That's bad enough.

650
00:42:44,395 --> 00:42:47,058
But you're being divorced,
looking for a nice settlement.

651
00:42:47,198 --> 00:42:48,996
When word of your
adultery got out,

652
00:42:49,133 --> 00:42:51,432
that would hurt your cause
pretty good, wouldn't it?

653
00:42:51,569 --> 00:42:53,868
I am still in the
middle of a divorce.

654
00:42:54,005 --> 00:42:56,804
I know. I know. I know.
You have the most to lose.

655
00:42:56,941 --> 00:42:59,536
That's why I think
you killed Dr. Fletcher.

656
00:42:59,677 --> 00:43:01,703
You wanted to
destroy those files,

657
00:43:01,846 --> 00:43:04,213
but you didn't have time
to open the safe there,

658
00:43:04,348 --> 00:43:07,546
so you took the safe
to your apartment,

659
00:43:07,685 --> 00:43:10,245
got it opened, and
destroyed the files, didn't you?

660
00:43:10,388 --> 00:43:12,619
No, I told you, I was
at the "wives only"...

661
00:43:12,757 --> 00:43:15,317
"Wives only" seminar.
I know. I know.

662
00:43:15,460 --> 00:43:18,658
You were there for
a while, but you left.

663
00:43:19,697 --> 00:43:23,327
When everybody came back
after coffee break at the seminar...

664
00:43:25,036 --> 00:43:32,500
Dr. Relkin passed out
these questionnaires.

665
00:43:32,643 --> 00:43:35,545
Everybody filled them
out and signed them.

666
00:43:35,680 --> 00:43:38,844
Your name appears nowhere
on these questionnaires.

667
00:43:38,983 --> 00:43:40,076
Why?

668
00:43:40,218 --> 00:43:42,881
Dr. Relkin must have lost it.

669
00:43:43,020 --> 00:43:46,616
Miss Powell, you can
remove the safe now.

670
00:43:46,757 --> 00:43:53,755
Dr. Relkin told me that she picked up
and numbered all of these questionnaires.

671
00:43:53,898 --> 00:43:55,696
Why isn't your name on here?

672
00:43:55,833 --> 00:43:58,496
Well, how should I know? It
could have fallen on the floor.

673
00:43:58,636 --> 00:44:01,936
Oh, I'm sorry, Miss Powell.
You need help. Could you...

674
00:44:05,710 --> 00:44:07,042
Officer?

675
00:44:17,355 --> 00:44:18,516
That's interesting.

676
00:44:18,656 --> 00:44:19,715
Excuse me.

677
00:44:19,857 --> 00:44:24,090
It takes not one, not two, but
three women to move that safe.

678
00:44:24,228 --> 00:44:26,891
You can put it down
now, thank you.

679
00:44:27,031 --> 00:44:31,526
You couldn't possibly have moved
that safe by yourself, could you?

680
00:44:31,669 --> 00:44:35,629
It took three women
to move that safe.

681
00:44:35,773 --> 00:44:38,800
Dr. Fletcher was
shot three times.

682
00:44:38,943 --> 00:44:44,143
Three women killed him: you,
Ginny Morell, Laura Corning.

683
00:44:44,282 --> 00:44:46,183
- Your Honor...
- Besides your questionnaire,

684
00:44:46,317 --> 00:44:50,846
two other questionnaires are missing...
Ginny Morell and Laura Corning.

685
00:44:50,988 --> 00:44:52,923
You left early, didn't you?

686
00:44:53,057 --> 00:44:56,653
Went over to Dr. Fletcher's, killed
him, and then you removed the safe.

687
00:44:56,794 --> 00:44:58,695
Objection, Your Honor.

688
00:44:58,829 --> 00:45:01,458
- Mr. Matlock.
- One more question.

689
00:45:01,599 --> 00:45:04,034
Are you going to take the
blame for this murder alone,

690
00:45:04,168 --> 00:45:08,663
or are you going to admit that
what I just said really happened?

691
00:45:08,806 --> 00:45:11,469
It's up to you, Mrs. Hertz.

692
00:45:27,024 --> 00:45:28,390
I can't thank you enough, Ben.

693
00:45:28,526 --> 00:45:30,119
Just keep selling insurance.

694
00:45:30,261 --> 00:45:31,957
Well, I can't for a while.

695
00:45:32,096 --> 00:45:33,826
Why the hell not?

696
00:45:33,965 --> 00:45:37,629
You've got to understand, Ben, my
wife was deceiving me with our therapist,

697
00:45:37,768 --> 00:45:39,608
and I've been tried for
murder, and she did it.

698
00:45:39,637 --> 00:45:42,505
My new therapist says that anyone
else would be dead from the stress,

699
00:45:42,640 --> 00:45:45,405
- and I will be, too, if I don't...
- What?

700
00:45:45,543 --> 00:45:49,105
Go away for a while,
a long while. Nature.

701
00:45:49,247 --> 00:45:51,739
Don't get me wrong,
Ben, I'll pay you.

702
00:45:51,882 --> 00:45:53,214
Good.

703
00:45:53,351 --> 00:45:55,650
It may take me years,
maybe the rest of my life.

704
00:45:55,786 --> 00:45:57,584
The rest of your life?

705
00:45:57,722 --> 00:46:00,521
Ben, people are living
longer and longer.

706
00:46:00,658 --> 00:46:04,356
I was at a seminar last
year... Wait, two years ago...

707
00:46:04,495 --> 00:46:06,225
It was in June...
no wait, July...

708
00:46:06,364 --> 00:46:08,364
And they said that men
are living into their 90s...

709
00:46:08,466 --> 00:46:11,732
Wait, wait... women are living
into their 90s and men into their 80s.

710
00:46:11,869 --> 00:46:14,029
You know, a nonsmoker like
you, well, then, you know...

9999
00:00:0,500 --> 00:00:2,00
